          "text": "Vanilla Layer Cake \u2014 concise recipe note\n\nForm\n- Two 8-inch (20 cm) round cake layers (9-inch acceptable); 2\u20133 layers possible with adjusted bake time.\n\nIngredients (makes 2 \u00d7 8\" layers)\n- 2 1/2 cups (312 g) all-purpose flour\n- 1 1/2 cups (300 g) granulated sugar\n- 2 1/2 tsp baking powder\n- 1/2 tsp salt\n- 1 cup (227 g) unsalted butter, softened\n- 4 large eggs, room temp\n- 1 cup (240 ml) whole milk, room temp\n- 2 tsp pure vanilla extract\n\nBasic method\n1. Preheat oven to 350\u00b0F (175\u00b0C). Grease and line pans.\n2. Whisk flour, baking powder, salt. Cream butter and sugar until pale; add eggs one at a time, then vanilla.\n3. Alternate adding flour mixture and milk in three additions, beginning and ending with flour; mix until just combined.\n4. Divide batter evenly into pans. Smooth tops.\n\nBaking time and doneness\n- Bake 25\u201330 minutes for 8\" rounds (30\u201335 for 9\"). Done when center springs back and a toothpick comes out with a few moist crumbs.\n- Cool in pans 10 minutes, then transfer to a rack to cool completely before frosting.\n\nStructure and handling\n- Expect a tender, fine crumb that holds filling and frosting well. Cool fully to avoid melting frosting. For clean layers, level domes before stacking. Apply a thin crumb coat, chill, then finish with final frosting.\n\nVanilla Buttercream Frosting (simple)\n- 1 cup (227 g) unsalted butter, softened\n- 3\u20134 cups (360\u2013480 g) powdered sugar, sifted\n- 2\u20133 tbsp heavy cream or milk\n- 1 1/2 tsp vanilla extract\n- Pinch salt\nBeat butter until smooth, add powdered sugar gradually, add cream and vanilla to reach spreadable consistency, and adjust salt.\n\nAssembly\n- Place one layer, spread even layer of frosting or filling, stack, crumb coat, chill 15\u201330 minutes, then apply final coat and decorate.\n\nStorage\n- Store covered at room temperature 1\u20132 days, or refrigerate up to 5 days (bring to room temp before serving)."
