          "text": "Vanilla Cake \u2013 Recipe Note\n\nForm & Structure  \n- Standard 2-layer round cake (2 x 8-inch pans) or 9x13-inch sheet cake.  \n- Aim for a tight, even crumb that slices cleanly and supports frosting.\n\nIngredients (basic ratio)  \n- 2\u00bd cups (300 g) all-purpose flour  \n- 2\u00bd tsp baking powder  \n- \u00bd tsp fine salt  \n- 1 cup (225 g) unsalted butter, room temp  \n- 1\u00be cups (350 g) granulated sugar  \n- 4 large eggs, room temp  \n- 1 Tbsp vanilla extract  \n- 1 cup (240 ml) whole milk, room temp (or half milk/half sour cream for extra tenderness)\n\nMethod & Baking Time  \n1. Preheat oven to 350\u00b0F (175\u00b0C). Grease and line pans with parchment.  \n2. Whisk flour, baking powder, and salt.  \n3. Beat butter and sugar until pale and fluffy (3\u20135 minutes).  \n4. Beat in eggs one at a time, then vanilla.  \n5. Add dry ingredients in 3 additions, alternating with milk in 2 additions, starting and ending with dry. Mix just until combined.  \n6. Divide batter evenly between pans, level tops.  \n7. Bake:  \n   - 8-inch rounds: 25\u201330 minutes  \n   - 9x13-inch: 30\u201335 minutes  \n   Done when a toothpick comes out clean and the top springs back.  \n8. Cool in pans 10 minutes, then turn out onto racks and cool completely before frosting.\n\nFrosting (simple vanilla buttercream)  \n- 1 cup (225 g) unsalted butter, room temp  \n- 3\u20134 cups (360\u2013480 g) powdered sugar, sifted  \n- 2\u20133 Tbsp milk or cream  \n- 1\u20132 tsp vanilla extract  \nBeat butter until smooth, gradually add powdered sugar, then vanilla and enough milk/cream to reach a spreadable consistency. Frost cooled cake; crumb-coat first for cleaner layers."
