          "text": "Vanilla Cake \u2013 Practical Recipe Note\n\nForm & Structure  \n- Standard 8-inch (20 cm) round layer cake, 2 layers.  \n- Creaming method for a fine, even crumb and good slicing structure.\n\nIngredients (cake)  \n- 1\u00bd cups (190 g) all-purpose flour  \n- 1\u00bd tsp baking powder  \n- \u00bc tsp fine salt  \n- \u00bd cup (115 g) unsalted butter, softened  \n- 1 cup (200 g) granulated sugar  \n- 2 large eggs, room temperature  \n- 2 tsp vanilla extract  \n- \u00bd cup (120 ml) whole milk, room temperature  \n- \u00bc cup (60 ml) sour cream or plain yogurt (for moisture and tenderness)\n\nIngredients (vanilla frosting)  \n- \u00bd cup (115 g) unsalted butter, softened  \n- 2\u20132\u00bd cups (240\u2013300 g) powdered sugar, sifted  \n- 1\u20132 tbsp milk or cream  \n- 1\u20132 tsp vanilla extract  \n- Pinch of salt\n\nMethod & Baking Time  \n1. Preheat oven to 350\u00b0F (175\u00b0C). Grease and line two 8-inch round pans.  \n2. Whisk flour, baking powder, and salt.  \n3. Beat butter and sugar until pale and fluffy (3\u20134 minutes).  \n4. Beat in eggs one at a time, then vanilla.  \n5. Mix milk and sour cream.  \n6. Add dry ingredients to butter mixture in 2\u20133 additions, alternating with milk mixture. End with dry. Mix just until combined.  \n7. Divide batter between pans, level tops.  \n8. Bake 22\u201328 minutes, until a toothpick comes out clean and tops spring back. Cool 10 minutes in pans, then fully on a rack.\n\nFrosting & Assembly  \n1. Beat butter until smooth. Add powdered sugar gradually, then vanilla, salt, and enough milk/cream for a spreadable consistency.  \n2. Level cake layers if domed.  \n3. Place first layer on a board, spread frosting, top with second layer.  \n4. Apply a thin crumb coat, chill 15\u201320 minutes, then finish with a smooth final coat."
