          "text": "Vanilla Cake \u2013 Practical Recipe Note\n\nForm & Structure  \n- Standard 2-layer round cake (2 x 8-inch / 20 cm pans) or 1 rectangular 9x13-inch pan.  \n- Aim for a tight, even crumb that slices cleanly and supports frosting without crumbling.\n\nIngredients (cake)  \n- 2\u00bd cups (300 g) all-purpose flour  \n- 2\u00bd tsp baking powder  \n- \u00bd tsp fine salt  \n- 1\u00be cups (350 g) granulated sugar  \n- \u00be cup (170 g) unsalted butter, room temp  \n- 3 large eggs, room temp  \n- 1 cup (240 ml) whole milk, room temp  \n- 2 tsp vanilla extract  \n\nIngredients (vanilla buttercream)  \n- 1 cup (225 g) unsalted butter, room temp  \n- 3\u20134 cups (360\u2013480 g) powdered sugar, sifted  \n- 2\u20133 tbsp milk or cream  \n- 1\u00bd\u20132 tsp vanilla extract  \n- Pinch of salt  \n\nMethod & Baking Time  \n1. Preheat oven to 350\u00b0F / 175\u00b0C. Grease and line pans with parchment.  \n2. Whisk flour, baking powder, and salt.  \n3. Beat butter and sugar until pale and fluffy (about 3\u20134 minutes).  \n4. Beat in eggs one at a time, then vanilla.  \n5. Add dry ingredients in 3 additions, alternating with milk, starting and ending with dry. Mix just until combined.  \n6. Divide batter evenly between pans, level tops.  \n7. Bake:  \n   - 8-inch rounds: 25\u201330 minutes  \n   - 9x13-inch: 30\u201335 minutes  \n   Done when a toothpick comes out clean and the top springs back.  \n8. Cool in pans 10 minutes, then turn out onto racks and cool completely.\n\nFrosting & Assembly  \n1. Beat butter until smooth. Gradually add powdered sugar, then vanilla, salt, and enough milk/cream to reach a spreadable but stable consistency.  \n2. Level cake tops if domed.  \n3. Place first layer on a board, spread an even layer of frosting.  \n4. Add second layer, crumb-coat the whole cake (thin layer of frosting), chill 15\u201320 minutes.  \n5. Apply final coat of frosting, smoothing sides and top. Store covered at cool room temperature for 1\u20132 days or refrigerate if very warm."
